    "sourceWikitext": "{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Sauce recipes\n| Difficulty = 1\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\nThis yogurt sauce is good for gyros, as a grilling baste for lamb and pork, and a dipping sauce for chips.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n*1 ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] plain [[Cookbook:Yogurt|yogurt]]\n*¼ cup freshly-squeezed [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]] juice\n*¼ cup extra-virgin [[Cookbook:Olive oil|olive oil]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] dried [[Cookbook:Oregano|oregano]]\n*1 tbsp minced [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n*Freshly-ground black [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]] to taste\n*¼ [[Cookbook:Each|ea]]. small red [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], finely [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n*1 ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] fresh [[Cookbook:Rosemary|rosemary]], finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*2 tbsp flat-leaf [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]], finely chopped\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Pulse all ingredients in a [[Cookbook:Food Processor|food processor]] until relatively smooth.\n#Pour into your dipping bowl, and serve with a Greek-style dish.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using yogurt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments]]\n[[Category:Greek recipes]]",
    "isRecipe": true,
